1
00:03:05,636 --> 00:03:07,728
<v MAN> Greek Island Holidays, can I help you?

2
00:03:07,728 --> 00:03:18,214
<v WOMAN> Yes, I hope so. I have a friend who's just come back from Corfu and she's recommended some apartments in Arilas. She thought they might be on your list.

3
00:03:18,214 --> 00:03:24,165
<v MAN> Arilas, Arilas, let me see. Can you give me the names?

4
00:03:24,165 --> 00:03:31,616
<v WOMAN> Yes, the first's Rose Garden Apartments. I'd like to go with another friend in the last week of October.

5
00:03:31,616 --> 00:03:42,153
<v MAN> Well, we've got a lovely studio flat available at that time. I'm sure you'd enjoy the entertainment programme there too, with Greek dancing in the restaurant.

6
00:03:42,153 --> 00:03:44,523
<v WOMAN> And the cost for each of us?

7
00:03:44,523 --> 00:03:46,853
<v MAN> ￡219.

8
00:03:46,853 --> 00:03:55,745
<v WOMAN> That sounds very reasonable!I'm just jotting down some notes. Now the second one she mentioned was called Blue Bay.

9
00:03:55,745 --> 00:04:03,574
<v MAN> Blue Bay? Yes, in fact that's very popular and it has some special features.

10
00:04:03,574 --> 00:04:04,107
<v WOMAN> Really?

11
00:04:04,107 --> 00:04:08,135
<v MAN> The main attraction is the large swimming pool with salt water.

12
00:04:08,135 --> 00:04:10,195
<v WOMAN> Much healthier, I understand.

13
00:04:10,195 --> 00:04:22,397
<v MAN> That's right. And it isn't far from the beach, either - only 300 metres, and only around half a kilometre to some shops, so you don't have to be too energetic.

14
00:04:22,397 --> 00:04:24,987
<v WOMAN> Is it much more expensive than the first one?

15
00:04:24,987 --> 00:04:35,955
<v MAN> Let me just check. I think at the time you want to go it's around ￡260 - no ￡275 to be exact.

16
00:04:35,955 --> 00:04:47,588
<v WOMAN> Right, I've got that. Now there are just two more apartments to ask you about. Um, I can't read my own writing! Something to do with sun... Sunshine, is it?

17
00:04:47,588 --> 00:04:52,064
<v MAN> I think you meant the Sunshade Apartments. They're on a mountainside.

18
00:04:52,064 --> 00:04:53,764
<v WOMAN> Any special features?

19
00:04:53,764 --> 00:04:59,489
<v MAN> Yes, each room has its own sun terrace and there are shared barbecue facilities.

20
00:04:59,489 --> 00:05:00,779
<v WOMAN> Sounds lovely!

21
00:05:00,779 --> 00:05:10,543
<v MAN> Yes, it is rather well-equipped.It also provides water sports - it has its own beach. There are facilities for water-skiing.

22
00:05:10,543 --> 00:05:13,422
<v WOMAN> Any kite-surfing? My friend's quite keen.

23
00:05:13,422 --> 00:05:20,885
<v MAN> Not at the hotel but I'm sure you'll find some in Arilas. There's also satellite TV in the apartments.

24
00:05:20,885 --> 00:05:22,764
<v WOMAN> And how much is that one?

25
00:05:22,764 --> 00:05:27,210
<v MAN> ￡490 with two sharing.

26
00:05:27,210 --> 00:05:29,928
<v WOMAN> You mean ￡245 each?

27
00:05:29,928 --> 00:05:36,616
<v MAN> I'm afraid not! Each person has to pay that amount and there must be at least two in an apartment.

28
00:05:36,616 --> 00:05:44,159
<v WOMAN> I don't think that would be within our budget, unfortunately. And the last one sounds a bit expensive too - the Grand!

29
00:05:44,159 --> 00:05:47,159
<v MAN> Actually it's quite reasonable. It's an older style house with Greek paintings in every room, and a balcony outside.

30
00:05:47,159 --> 00:05:54,734
<v WOMAN> Sound nice. What are the views like?

31
00:05:54,734 --> 00:06:05,365
<v MAN> Well, there are forests all round and they hide a supermarket just dow the road, so that's very useful for all your shopping needs. There's a disco in the area too.

32
00:06:05,365 --> 00:06:06,386
<v WOMAN> And the price?

33
00:06:06,386 --> 00:06:14,268
<v MAN> ￡319 at that time, but if you leave it till November it goes down by 40%.

34
00:06:14,268 --> 00:06:16,345
<v WOMAN> Too late, I'm afraid.

35
00:06:16,345 --> 00:06:21,231
<v MAN> Well, why don't i send you a brochure with full details, Ms...?

36
00:06:21,231 --> 00:06:28,820
<v WOMAN> Nash. But don't worry about that.I'm coming to Upminster soon and I'll call and get one. I just wanted to get an idea first.

37
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:32,783
<v MAN> Well, that's fine. We've got plenty here when you come.

38
00:07:20,549 --> 00:07:28,993
<v WOMAN> If you've got a minute, could I just check a couple of points about insurance? I got one policy through the post but I'd like to see if yours is better.

39
00:07:28,993 --> 00:07:31,773
<v MAN> Fine. What would you like to know?

40
00:07:31,773 --> 00:07:38,259
<v WOMAN> Well, the one I've got has benefits and then the maximum amount you can claim. Is that like yours?

41
00:07:38,259 --> 00:07:41,208
<v MAN> Yes, that's how most of them are.

42
00:07:41,208 --> 00:07:48,368
<v WOMAN> Well, the first thing is cancellation.If the holiday's cancelled on the policy I've got, you can claim ￡8,000.

43
00:07:48,368 --> 00:07:55,601
<v MAN> We can improve on that, Ms Nash. For Greek Island holidays, our maximum is ￡10,000

44
00:07:55,601 --> 00:08:00,799
<v WOMAN> That's good - of course our holiday won't even cost ￡1,000 together!

45
00:08:00,799 --> 00:08:07,566
<v MAN> It's still sensible to have good cover. Now, if you go to hospital, we allow ￡600. 

46
00:08:07,566 --> 00:08:08,572
<v WOMAN> Yes, mine's similar.

47
00:08:08,572 --> 00:08:12,636
<v MAN> And we also allow a relative to travel to your holiday resort.

48
00:08:12,636 --> 00:08:16,662
<v WOMAN> My policy just says their representative will help you.

49
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:21,476
<v MAN> You can see there's another difference there. And what happens if you don't get on the plane?

50
00:08:21,476 --> 00:08:24,691
<v WOMAN> Nothing, as far as I can see on this form.

51
00:08:24,691 --> 00:08:28,173
<v MAN> Don't you have missed departure?

52
00:08:28,173 --> 00:08:31,410
<v WOMAN> No, I'll just jot that down.

53
00:08:31,410 --> 00:08:45,099
<v MAN> We pay up to ￡1,000 for that, depending on the reason. And we're particularly generous about loss of personal belongings - up to ￡3,000, but not more than ￡500 for a single item.

54
00:08:45,099 --> 00:08:47,381
<v WOMAN> Then I'd better not take my laptop!

55
00:08:47,381 --> 00:08:49,503
<v MAN> Not unless you insure it separately.

56
00:08:49,503 --> 00:08:55,704
<v WOMAN> OK - thanks very much for your time - you've really been helpful. Can I get back to you? Your name is?

57
00:08:55,704 --> 00:09:14,169
<v MAN> Ben - Ludlow.That's L-U-D-L-O-W. I'm the Assistant Manager here. I'll give you my number. It's 081260 543216.

58
00:09:14,169 --> 00:09:23,226
<v WOMAN> But didn't phone 08126 567294? That's what I've got on the paper.

59
00:09:23,226 --> 00:09:26,518
<v MAN> That's the main switchboard. I've given you my direct line.

60
00:09:26,518 --> 00:09:28,991
<v WOMAN> Right, thank you...